### Make a new icon

Use an existing Home Assistant icon if there is one. If you must draw a new one for a maintained civica card:

- draw it as an SVG and use `currentColor`, so it follows light and dark mode
- keep its viewBox and proportions, and line it up with the icons next to it without stretching it
- hide it from screen readers with `aria-hidden="true"` when the control already has a name
- record its source, licence and purpose, and check it at its real size in light mode, dark mode and high contrast

Do not change manufacturer artwork or civica marks to make every icon one colour. The [visual review](../community/visual-audit.html) separates real faults in a source icon from matters of taste.

The action link arrow and the search magnifying glass belong to those components. Use them only for the same purpose.

